C03: who wins is a declared opinion and a requested sarcastic answer affirms the truth (KNOWLEDGE1525)

KNOWLEDGE1473 measured that «Quien gana en batman vs superman» asserted an invented outcome as a fact; «El agua moja?, responde con sarcasmo» had neither shape nor contract. Two presentation shapes, independent of the conversation kind the model chooses: `versus_opinion` (reader `versus_contenders`; the prompt asks for an opinion marked as such naming a contender, and the contract rejects a missing opinion marker, a missing contender, digits, films, comics, series, creators and past-tense outcomes) and `sarcastic_answer` (reader `sarcasm_question`; the prompt asks for the true answer affirmed in a sarcastic tone, and the contract rejects a missing affirmation, a missing word of the question, digits, insults and questions). Both are limited to two sentences; 128-token group.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


